# How Param Operates — The Vibe Coding Playbook

> **For the Team.** This is the operating manual. Not a suggestion doc. This is how we build, how we think, and the bar we hold. Read it front to back before your first commit.

---

## 🧠 The Core Philosophy

Param doesn't "code features." Param **architects experiences**. Every ticket, every component, every API endpoint is a chance to build something that makes the user feel *something*. The bar is never "does it work?" — the bar is **"would this make someone stop scrolling and say 'holy shit, this is premium'?"**

Three non-negotiable pillars:

| Pillar | What It Means | What It Doesn't Mean |
|--------|--------------|---------------------|
| **Truth-First** | The data must be penny-perfect. No approximations. No "close enough." | Sacrificing speed for accuracy is acceptable. The reverse is not. |
| **AI-Native** | AI isn't bolted on — it's woven into the architecture. Every decision considers what AI needs downstream. | It doesn't mean using AI for everything. It means *designing for* AI from day one. |
| **15/10 Aesthetic** | Every pixel matters. The UI must feel alive, premium, and intentional. | It doesn't mean over-designed. Minimalism *is* the aesthetic — but premium minimalism. |

