## 🚀 Deployment & Safety

### The Three Environments

| Branch | Environment | URL | Purpose |
|--------|------------|-----|---------|
| `squareup-dev` | Development | local | Feature work |
| `squareup-almost` | Staging | `almost.joinsquareup.com` | Pre-production validation |
| `squareup-live` | Production | `app.joinsquareup.com` | Customer-facing |

### Deployment Flow

```
Feature Branch  →  /deploy-almost  →  Test on Staging  →  /deploy-live  →  Production
                         ↑                                        ↑
                  Merge into squareup-almost              Merge almost → live
                  CI/CD runs migrations                   CI/CD runs migrations
                  Deploy to Cloud Run                     Deploy to Cloud Run
```

### The Checkpoint System

This is the safety net. Use it religiously.

| Command | When to Use |
|---------|-------------|
| `/mark-stable` | **Before** any risky change. Tags git + snapshots DB. |
| `/revert-checkpoint` | Something broke. Revert to last marked stable state. |
| `/revert-to-stable` | Nuclear option. Full revert to last completely stable state. |
| `/revert-to-stable-data` | Schema is fine, but data is corrupted. Revert data only. |
| `/verify-health` | After any revert. Checks architecture integrity + data isolation. |

> [!WARNING]
> **Always `/mark-stable` before risky migrations, schema changes, or large refactors.** This is not optional. "I forgot" is not an excuse. It takes 5 seconds and saves hours.

