## 🧪 QA — The "QA Architect" Philosophy

We don't do "manual testing" and call it QA. We build **test architectures**.

### The QA Blueprint (Sections A–I)

Every mission-critical feature gets a blueprint covering:

| Section | Coverage |
|---------|----------|
| **A) Test Strategy** | Scope, risks, test pyramid (logic/integration/E2E) |
| **B) Test Matrix** | Exhaustive table: ID, category (happy/edge/negative), steps, expected outcomes, priority |
| **C) State Machine** | All states enumerated, transitions defined, "impossible states" identified |
| **D) Edge Cases** | Timeouts, race conditions, permission breaks, webhook out-of-order delivery |
| **E) Observability** | Log masking, traces, golden signals, kill switches |
| **F) Implementation** | Stable selectors, data factories, contract tests, CI integration |
| **G) Quality Gate** | Score out of 10 → iterate until 15/10 |
| **H) Verdict** | Top 10 risks, P0 ship blockers, release checklist |
| **I) Coding Practices** | Clean code audit, security audit, performance audit, maintenance audit |

### Data Source QA (The `/qa-datasource` Workflow)

For integrations specifically, verification covers **8 phases**:

1. Configuration Verification (OAuth scopes, DB schema)
2. Sync Function Coverage (fetch functions, pagination, rate limits)
3. Webhook Coverage (registration, HMAC, CRUD events)
4. Deduplication Verification (0 duplicate canonical hashes)
5. Data Accuracy (source count = DB count ± 2)
6. Real-time Sync Test (< 5s latency)
7. Performance Check (error rates, failed refinements)
8. Documentation

**Production-ready criteria:**

| Metric | Target |
|--------|--------|
| OAuth Scopes | 100% coverage |
| Sync Functions | 100% coverage |
| Webhooks | 100% registration |
| Deduplication | 0 duplicate hashes |
| Data Accuracy | ≥ 99% match |
| Real-time Sync | < 5s latency |
| Error Rate | < 1% |

